- The key purpose of DAY1: to appear genuine, approachable, and non-commercial;
- Detailed guidance on profile setup emphasizing a balanced, realistic introduction without exaggeration or suggestiveness, with concrete examples;
- Instructions for the first post focusing on creating a safe, non-sensational impression using a sample greeting;
- An in-depth reply strategy targeting “oji-san” users who interact with female accounts, including how to identify suitable targets, reply templates for casual empathy, limits on engagement, and explicit avoidance of DM or meeting requests;
- Advice on managing replies to one’s own posts;
- A final DAY1 checklist for ensuring all tasks are completed.

I concluded by summarizing DAY1’s role as the foundation for building trust and engagement that enables progression to later stages like posting strategy and subtle teasing (DAY2–DAY3). I also prompted the user to choose which next section they want me to prepare first (DAY2–DAY3 content or overall action templates).

This integrated approach ensures readers can follow a clear, no-waste workflow from knowledge to action for DAY1, facilitating smooth execution and setting them up for successful growth in subsequent phases.
